<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Giovanni II Bentivoglio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1443–1508</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Giovanni II Bentivoglio was the effective ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bologna">Bologna</a> from 1463 to 1506, governing through the city's councils while keeping its formal ties to the Papal States. He was a patron of art and architecture. In 1506 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-julius-ii">Pope Julius II</a> marched on Bologna and drove him out, bringing the city under direct papal rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/giovanni-ii-bentivoglio.jpg" alt="Giovanni II Bentivoglio" width="320" height="464" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ercole de' Roberti · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ercole_de%27_Roberti_001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
